1
00:00:09,884 --> 00:00:11,636
[Rebecca] <i>I just can't shake this feeling.</i>

2
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:13,430
<i>This place isn't right. It's evil.</i>

3
00:00:14,681 --> 00:00:17,183
Crisanto has had a harder time of it
than I have.

4
00:00:17,267 --> 00:00:19,227
[flesh squelching]

5
00:00:19,936 --> 00:00:22,272
[Rebecca]
<i>Are you still dreaming about the island?</i>

6
00:00:23,648 --> 00:00:25,775
- [creature growls]
- [Rebecca shrieks]

7
00:00:25,859 --> 00:00:28,486
[Rebecca] <i>We need to find Sabina</i>
<i>and get off this island.</i>

8
00:00:28,570 --> 00:00:29,988
[woman screaming distantly]

9
00:00:33,950 --> 00:00:34,909
Sabina, run!

10
00:00:34,993 --> 00:00:38,288
[Diwa] <i>If you ever want to see your mother</i>
<i>again, you must go now.</i>

11
00:00:39,330 --> 00:00:41,499
- [creature snarling]
- [Ramon] What the fuck are you doing?

12
00:00:41,583 --> 00:00:43,376
[Javier] <i>You think you'll get out of here?</i>

13
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:45,045
<i>You'll rot on this island</i>
<i>like the rest of us.</i>

14
00:00:45,128 --> 00:00:46,880
- [Diwa] Señor, please.
- Your choice, then.

15
00:00:46,963 --> 00:00:48,465
[gunshots]

16
00:00:48,548 --> 00:00:49,591
- [gasps]
- [groans]

17
00:00:49,674 --> 00:00:51,926
[panting]

18
00:00:52,010 --> 00:00:54,095
- [Sabina] Ma?
- Sabina, we need to go.

19
00:00:54,679 --> 00:00:57,098
[yelps, growling]

20
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:00,101
[growl echoes]

21
00:01:00,727 --> 00:01:02,729
[gentle music playing]

22
00:01:31,841 --> 00:01:34,469
[indistinct chatter]

23
00:01:35,762 --> 00:01:36,971
[woman laughs]

24
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:42,602
- Is this the man running?
- Ma.

25
00:01:42,685 --> 00:01:45,980
How many times have you shown me
that picture? Who is he anyway?

26
00:01:53,530 --> 00:01:54,948
Okay, Ma. That's him.

27
00:01:55,031 --> 00:01:56,950
Well, then, aren't you bothered by that?

28
00:01:57,033 --> 00:01:59,661
- But, Ma, how can I…
- [cell phone ringing]

29
00:02:05,125 --> 00:02:07,001
You'll understand eventually.

30
00:02:07,085 --> 00:02:09,087
[cell phone continues ringing]

31
00:02:32,068 --> 00:02:34,070
[suspenseful music playing]

32
00:02:36,322 --> 00:02:41,119
DON'T LOOK FOR ME.
I LOVE YOU, SABINA.

33
00:02:46,749 --> 00:02:48,376
[footsteps depart]

34
00:03:14,152 --> 00:03:16,154
[music builds]

35
00:03:57,487 --> 00:03:59,489
[music grows sinister]

36
00:04:01,866 --> 00:04:03,868
[whimper echoing]

37
00:04:13,294 --> 00:04:15,296
[moaning]

38
00:04:19,133 --> 00:04:20,134
[gasps]

39
00:04:27,892 --> 00:04:28,726
[grunts]

40
00:04:44,867 --> 00:04:47,287
[breathing heavily]

41
00:04:48,663 --> 00:04:49,872
[shrieks]

42
00:04:52,542 --> 00:04:53,751
[groans loudly]

43
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:56,462
[panting]

44
00:04:58,339 --> 00:05:00,216
[old lady] So, you've come back.

45
00:05:02,176 --> 00:05:03,636
Don't you remember me?

46
00:05:05,888 --> 00:05:07,890
The island knew you would return.

47
00:05:09,642 --> 00:05:10,935
But why have you?

48
00:05:11,894 --> 00:05:13,021
For my brother.

49
00:05:14,856 --> 00:05:16,149
It's been so long.

50
00:05:17,525 --> 00:05:19,694
But I know in my heart he's alive.

51
00:05:20,611 --> 00:05:21,446
That is true.

52
00:05:23,531 --> 00:05:25,116
He's alive? Are you sure?

53
00:05:26,492 --> 00:05:29,579
Although, how do you plan
on leaving the island?

54
00:05:30,288 --> 00:05:32,623
The boat. There's no other way.

55
00:05:33,333 --> 00:05:35,418
It's not that easy, you know?

56
00:05:36,586 --> 00:05:40,923
I'm not sure how you did it before
and why the island let you leave.

57
00:05:41,007 --> 00:05:42,216
If I already did it,

58
00:05:43,301 --> 00:05:44,510
well, I can do it again.

59
00:05:46,637 --> 00:05:48,639
[sinister music playing]

60
00:05:56,606 --> 00:05:58,024
[ominous sting]

61
00:06:04,113 --> 00:06:06,115
- [creature growls]
- [inhales deeply]

62
00:06:07,283 --> 00:06:08,701
[exhales heavily]

63
00:06:30,598 --> 00:06:32,683
[ominous music playing]

64
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:36,062
[Rebecca breathes heavily]

65
00:07:01,379 --> 00:07:02,296
Vedasto.

66
00:07:11,973 --> 00:07:12,890
Brother.

67
00:07:13,891 --> 00:07:14,934
It's me, Becca.

68
00:07:17,478 --> 00:07:19,230
We're getting out of here.

69
00:07:21,649 --> 00:07:22,775
Where's Bryan?

70
00:07:24,026 --> 00:07:24,944
Where's Ding?

71
00:07:26,362 --> 00:07:27,447
Can you hear me?

72
00:07:28,656 --> 00:07:29,824
[man] That old man's your brother?

73
00:07:31,367 --> 00:07:33,536
I've never heard him speak a single word.

74
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:36,539
They say he has been here the longest,

75
00:07:36,622 --> 00:07:38,708
that the brothers
refused to kill him as punishment.

76
00:07:39,584 --> 00:07:41,794
I don't know
what they're planning to do to him.

77
00:07:42,545 --> 00:07:43,963
[Rebecca] What have they done to you?

78
00:07:44,046 --> 00:07:46,466
- [twigs snap]
- [Rebecca breathes heavily]

79
00:07:49,135 --> 00:07:51,137
[dramatic music plays]

80
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:56,476
[theme music playing]

81
00:09:00,581 --> 00:09:04,001
BALARAW: BLOOD ISLAND

82
00:09:17,306 --> 00:09:19,976
[Elsa]
Crisanto, what are we gonna eat now?

83
00:09:21,310 --> 00:09:24,522
We've lived perfectly fine
without those brothers before, right?

84
00:09:29,277 --> 00:09:30,945
We'll do so again, you'll see.

85
00:09:34,323 --> 00:09:35,241
[grunts softly]

86
00:09:39,036 --> 00:09:42,164
This is where Mina and I
used to hang out together. [cries]

87
00:09:48,337 --> 00:09:50,590
We will find your wife, Crisanto.

88
00:09:53,050 --> 00:09:54,844
It's been too long.

89
00:09:56,137 --> 00:09:57,388
I'll never find her.

90
00:10:02,059 --> 00:10:03,060
I hope for her…

91
00:10:05,688 --> 00:10:07,523
that she at least died painlessly.

92
00:10:13,362 --> 00:10:15,364
[eerie music playing]

93
00:10:31,130 --> 00:10:32,882
You came here with Sabina.

94
00:10:34,091 --> 00:10:36,052
You think you could escape us?

95
00:10:36,135 --> 00:10:37,970
Well, we outsmarted you.

96
00:10:38,054 --> 00:10:39,138
[Javier] Outsmarted, huh?

97
00:10:40,014 --> 00:10:43,976
Seems to me the smart one
wouldn't be locked up in a cage.

98
00:10:44,060 --> 00:10:46,228
We got inside your house.

99
00:10:46,312 --> 00:10:49,732
We saw the creature, you know,
the one you tied to the wall in there?

100
00:10:51,233 --> 00:10:52,318
Does everybody else know

101
00:10:52,401 --> 00:10:54,904
that you have that creature
hidden in there like a slave?

102
00:10:56,238 --> 00:10:57,156
Do you all know that?

103
00:10:58,949 --> 00:11:00,576
They have no idea, right?

104
00:11:01,744 --> 00:11:02,828
Vedasto!

105
00:11:13,714 --> 00:11:16,509
- [Arturo grunts]
- Sarge! Sarge! Stop! Sarge!

106
00:11:17,259 --> 00:11:19,053
- [groans]
- Sarge!

107
00:11:19,136 --> 00:11:21,639
Stop hitting him! Let me go!

108
00:11:22,223 --> 00:11:24,183
[groans]

109
00:11:24,266 --> 00:11:25,643
[Bulak grunts angrily]

110
00:11:26,352 --> 00:11:27,269
Sarge!

111
00:11:33,359 --> 00:11:35,361
[Bulak grunts, breathes heavily]

112
00:11:35,945 --> 00:11:36,821
Sarge?

113
00:11:38,406 --> 00:11:39,907
Sarge, you okay?

114
00:11:45,287 --> 00:11:46,914
Sarge, let me see.

115
00:11:48,207 --> 00:11:49,458
[grunts loudly]

116
00:11:51,168 --> 00:11:52,920
[straining]

117
00:11:56,799 --> 00:11:58,134
[Rebecca groaning]

118
00:12:06,517 --> 00:12:09,478
Just hold on, Ma. I'll get us out of here.

119
00:12:11,647 --> 00:12:12,565
[Crisanto] Señor.

120
00:12:13,399 --> 00:12:15,359
Señor, was she telling the truth?

121
00:12:17,111 --> 00:12:18,028
Huh?

122
00:12:19,655 --> 00:12:21,157
That you're hiding a creature.

123
00:12:25,286 --> 00:12:28,622
Everyone who turned into those creatures,
we buried them all, didn't we?

124
00:12:30,374 --> 00:12:31,667
Not everyone.

125
00:12:33,794 --> 00:12:37,006
Crisanto, no one knows
what actually took your wife.

126
00:12:38,966 --> 00:12:42,303
Tell you what, you come by my house later,
and I'll bring you in.

127
00:12:43,596 --> 00:12:47,349
You can check every corner of my house,
and let's see if you find anything.

128
00:12:48,142 --> 00:12:52,605
You don't want to let yourself believe
in the crazy stories of these outsiders.

129
00:12:52,688 --> 00:12:54,482
Don't be so gullible.

130
00:12:54,565 --> 00:12:57,610
See for yourself anytime you want to.

131
00:12:58,861 --> 00:13:00,070
Forgive me, Señor.

132
00:13:06,702 --> 00:13:07,536
[grunts softly]

133
00:13:29,308 --> 00:13:32,061
Andres served this island for a long time.

134
00:13:35,397 --> 00:13:36,690
Served us all.

135
00:13:39,527 --> 00:13:42,738
He put his soul
into the work that he did every day

136
00:13:45,574 --> 00:13:47,076
to make sure we could live

137
00:13:48,494 --> 00:13:50,120
a peaceful life here.

138
00:13:50,204 --> 00:13:52,206
[ominous music playing]

139
00:13:54,625 --> 00:13:56,835
[breath trembling] Gather close.

140
00:14:01,966 --> 00:14:03,467
[sniffles]

141
00:14:05,261 --> 00:14:07,137
It's been so long since I lost…

142
00:14:08,556 --> 00:14:09,807
a relative.

143
00:14:12,851 --> 00:14:14,687
A family member, a loved one.

144
00:14:16,397 --> 00:14:17,606
[sobs softly]

145
00:14:22,861 --> 00:14:25,155
I've forgotten the pain of the sorrow.

146
00:14:26,448 --> 00:14:27,283
[sobs]

147
00:14:28,742 --> 00:14:30,744
The pain of grief and loss.

148
00:14:37,751 --> 00:14:39,753
It's almost too much to bear.

149
00:14:45,259 --> 00:14:48,470
Now I find
the thing that hurts most of all

150
00:14:49,221 --> 00:14:50,431
is my anger.

151
00:14:55,185 --> 00:14:58,188
Andres was taken from us far too soon.

152
00:15:03,819 --> 00:15:05,321
Those responsible…

153
00:15:08,282 --> 00:15:09,783
They will be found,

154
00:15:12,286 --> 00:15:13,370
and they will pay.

155
00:15:18,751 --> 00:15:20,127
[sniffles]

156
00:15:39,271 --> 00:15:41,273
[music builds]

157
00:15:52,826 --> 00:15:53,869
- [grunts]
- [flesh squelches]

158
00:16:06,256 --> 00:16:07,091
[sobs softly]

159
00:16:53,804 --> 00:16:55,806
[flesh squelching]

160
00:17:32,009 --> 00:17:34,011
[breath trembling]

161
00:18:23,936 --> 00:18:26,355
[Ramon] Seems like
you were getting all soft on us.

162
00:18:28,357 --> 00:18:29,900
We shouldn't have done that to Andres.

163
00:18:29,983 --> 00:18:32,778
We should have buried him.
Are we no different to them?

164
00:18:34,363 --> 00:18:36,365
If you had just been more careful,

165
00:18:36,448 --> 00:18:38,158
we could have avoided
this whole situation.

166
00:18:38,242 --> 00:18:39,618
Are you blaming me?

167
00:18:40,244 --> 00:18:43,664
When I think that you were there…
And you should have done more.

168
00:18:43,747 --> 00:18:46,250
It was your responsibility
to make sure that nothing--

169
00:18:46,333 --> 00:18:48,544
[Rafael] Stop! This is pointless.

170
00:18:50,879 --> 00:18:55,717
The most important thing right now is that
we find those who are truly responsible.

171
00:18:59,471 --> 00:19:04,852
We cannot let our life on this island
be damaged by those outsiders.

172
00:19:04,935 --> 00:19:06,311
This mother and daughter.

173
00:19:07,604 --> 00:19:09,273
I'll take care of that.

174
00:19:09,815 --> 00:19:11,650
You have one last chance.

175
00:19:11,733 --> 00:19:15,529
You bring Diwa, Sabina,
and Rebecca back home alive!

176
00:19:16,155 --> 00:19:17,072
Why?

177
00:19:18,323 --> 00:19:21,201
Are you sure that woman is your daughter?

178
00:19:21,285 --> 00:19:23,871
And you still believe
Rebecca would come back?

179
00:19:23,954 --> 00:19:26,456
Diwa is a traitor.
We should just kill them all!

180
00:19:26,540 --> 00:19:27,624
Javier, think about it.

181
00:19:27,708 --> 00:19:31,211
If we kill them, our people will lose
even more trust in us.

182
00:19:31,295 --> 00:19:33,672
They think we'll kill
everyone we disagree with.

183
00:19:33,755 --> 00:19:35,549
No! Too many have already died.

184
00:19:35,632 --> 00:19:36,675
That's enough!

185
00:19:42,055 --> 00:19:43,056
[exhales shakily]

186
00:19:45,851 --> 00:19:48,187
[strains, panting]

187
00:19:50,063 --> 00:19:51,815
[creature screeches distantly]

188
00:19:52,482 --> 00:19:54,484
[continues panting]

189
00:19:59,531 --> 00:20:01,533
[sinister music playing]

190
00:20:56,797 --> 00:20:58,715
[man] <i>All of us, we want to be free.</i>

191
00:20:59,925 --> 00:21:01,343
But you two.

192
00:21:02,219 --> 00:21:04,638
You insisted on coming here willingly.

193
00:21:06,181 --> 00:21:07,599
What is the matter with you?

194
00:21:09,685 --> 00:21:11,603
What is it that they did to him?

195
00:21:13,480 --> 00:21:16,441
[man] I heard they drove him mad.

196
00:21:17,317 --> 00:21:20,570
He only listens to the Cardomas now,
as far as I know.

197
00:21:20,654 --> 00:21:21,571
Sarge?

198
00:21:42,259 --> 00:21:44,011
I'm a good friend of Rebecca's.

199
00:21:51,143 --> 00:21:52,894
She came a long way to get here.

200
00:21:54,688 --> 00:21:55,605
To save you.

201
00:21:59,776 --> 00:22:00,694
And me…

202
00:22:02,237 --> 00:22:03,739
I came here to save her.

203
00:22:05,365 --> 00:22:06,533
That's the whole tale.

204
00:22:14,291 --> 00:22:15,709
It was hell getting here.

205
00:22:16,793 --> 00:22:19,880
She went through hell
just to get back here to see you.

206
00:22:24,593 --> 00:22:26,678
She told me so many stories about you.

207
00:22:27,596 --> 00:22:28,513
She said

208
00:22:30,474 --> 00:22:31,975
that you were a big reason

209
00:22:32,059 --> 00:22:35,896
as to why she wanted to study
all the islands in the Philippines,

210
00:22:35,979 --> 00:22:38,398
especially all the unexplored ones.

211
00:22:40,692 --> 00:22:41,777
She also said

212
00:22:43,653 --> 00:22:45,447
that you're the one who would protect her,

213
00:22:45,530 --> 00:22:47,949
that you beat up a guy once
for harassing her.

214
00:22:48,742 --> 00:22:51,578
[chuckles] That you beat him real good.

215
00:22:58,085 --> 00:22:59,002
And once,

216
00:23:00,462 --> 00:23:02,089
back when you were just kids,

217
00:23:02,923 --> 00:23:05,342
your parents just up and left you guys.

218
00:23:07,385 --> 00:23:09,805
And it was you who took care of her.

219
00:23:13,683 --> 00:23:17,104
You were always there for her.
That's how she remembers it.

220
00:23:20,690 --> 00:23:23,527
She thought it was only right
to come back for you.

221
00:23:32,119 --> 00:23:34,454
[pensive music playing]

222
00:23:51,138 --> 00:23:53,140
[foreboding music playing]

223
00:23:55,350 --> 00:23:57,018
[breathes deeply]

224
00:24:09,072 --> 00:24:11,074
[foreboding music continues]

225
00:24:26,548 --> 00:24:28,550
[music builds]

226
00:24:42,731 --> 00:24:44,733
[creaking]

227
00:25:10,884 --> 00:25:11,718
[gasps]

228
00:25:31,696 --> 00:25:33,698
[breathing heavily]

229
00:25:40,121 --> 00:25:42,999
[Arturo] <i>Don't come near me!</i>
<i>Don't you dare come near me!</i>

230
00:25:43,083 --> 00:25:44,334
Uncle Art?

231
00:25:47,295 --> 00:25:49,714
- [Bulak] <i>Sabina? Sabina!</i>
- Bulak?

232
00:25:50,382 --> 00:25:52,217
Hey! Hey! Where are they?

233
00:25:52,842 --> 00:25:54,386
[breathing heavily]

234
00:25:54,469 --> 00:25:55,887
Where are you?

235
00:25:56,596 --> 00:25:57,806
Bulak!

236
00:25:58,515 --> 00:26:00,600
Uncle! [breathing heavily]

237
00:26:25,750 --> 00:26:26,584
[winces]

238
00:26:30,547 --> 00:26:31,381
[groans]

239
00:26:37,345 --> 00:26:39,347
[breathing heavily]

240
00:26:51,651 --> 00:26:52,652
Where's Crisanto?

241
00:26:53,862 --> 00:26:56,281
Señor, I can't find Crisanto at all.

242
00:26:57,532 --> 00:26:58,992
Where is that bastard?

243
00:26:59,075 --> 00:27:01,786
[guard] Somebody might have found
Señor Ramon's daughter.

244
00:27:01,870 --> 00:27:03,747
- You stay and guard the camp.
- Yes, Señor.

245
00:27:03,830 --> 00:27:04,914
You two follow me.

246
00:27:08,793 --> 00:27:10,795
[suspenseful music playing]

247
00:27:25,477 --> 00:27:27,479
[Rafael snoring]

248
00:28:05,392 --> 00:28:07,394
[snoring continues]

249
00:28:29,165 --> 00:28:30,917
[clears throat]

250
00:28:34,754 --> 00:28:36,297
[wood creaking]

251
00:28:50,645 --> 00:28:52,647
[metal rattling]

252
00:29:41,696 --> 00:29:42,906
[creature snarls]

253
00:30:24,697 --> 00:30:25,698
[gulps]

254
00:30:32,413 --> 00:30:33,915
Mina, is that you?

255
00:30:46,803 --> 00:30:47,720
Mina.

256
00:30:49,013 --> 00:30:51,015
[Crisanto breathing shakily]

257
00:30:57,230 --> 00:30:58,231
[Crisanto whimpers]

258
00:31:22,338 --> 00:31:24,757
[breathing heavily, gulps]

259
00:31:31,347 --> 00:31:33,433
- [Crisanto grunts]
- [Mina howls]

260
00:31:35,643 --> 00:31:37,645
[melancholy music playing]

261
00:31:45,945 --> 00:31:47,947
[Crisanto sobbing softly]

262
00:32:01,419 --> 00:32:02,503
[Crisanto grunts]

263
00:32:04,547 --> 00:32:06,799
[Crisanto sobbing]

264
00:32:32,951 --> 00:32:35,286
[sinister music playing]

265
00:32:50,718 --> 00:32:51,928
[male voice] <i>Sabina.</i>

266
00:32:58,059 --> 00:32:59,060
<i>Wake up.</i>

267
00:33:09,404 --> 00:33:10,613
<i>Get up, Sabina.</i>

268
00:33:28,006 --> 00:33:30,008
[foreboding music playing]

269
00:33:36,472 --> 00:33:37,473
<i>Sabina.</i>

270
00:33:39,392 --> 00:33:40,601
<i>My daughter.</i>

271
00:33:47,442 --> 00:33:49,944
<i>The waves have brought you here</i>
<i>for a reason.</i>

272
00:33:54,949 --> 00:33:56,701
<i>This is where you belong.</i>

273
00:33:57,577 --> 00:33:59,579
[creaking]

274
00:34:01,789 --> 00:34:02,790
<i>My blood…</i>

275
00:34:06,044 --> 00:34:07,128
<i>and yours…</i>

276
00:34:10,590 --> 00:34:11,799
<i>are one.</i>

277
00:34:16,095 --> 00:34:17,513
<i>Now that you're home…</i>

278
00:34:21,809 --> 00:34:25,146
<i>the time has come</i>
<i>for this blood to be shared by all.</i>

279
00:34:29,400 --> 00:34:31,027
<i>We will multiply</i>

280
00:34:32,028 --> 00:34:33,237
<i>and conquer.</i>

281
00:34:35,031 --> 00:34:39,118
<i>One must remain. Another must sacrifice.</i>

282
00:34:41,496 --> 00:34:42,705
<i>Are you prepared?</i>

283
00:34:43,706 --> 00:34:44,957
- [gasps]
- [creature snarls]

284
00:34:49,170 --> 00:34:51,172
[breathing heavily]

285
00:35:39,137 --> 00:35:40,304
Where are we?

286
00:35:54,986 --> 00:35:56,070
Who are you?

287
00:35:58,072 --> 00:35:59,907
Don't worry yourself.

288
00:35:59,991 --> 00:36:02,410
The Cardomas don't come into this area.

289
00:36:04,954 --> 00:36:08,624
They don't come in here
because they know I don't answer to them.

290
00:36:08,708 --> 00:36:09,917
They know it.

291
00:36:11,544 --> 00:36:13,045
I'm a separate person.

292
00:36:14,797 --> 00:36:18,259
I refuse to live out my days as a slave
like the rest of them.

293
00:36:20,261 --> 00:36:22,638
Why haven't you left the island, then?

294
00:36:22,722 --> 00:36:25,683
Nobody leaves this island, my girl.

295
00:36:25,766 --> 00:36:27,351
But your mother seemed able to.

296
00:36:28,186 --> 00:36:29,145
Is she still alive?

297
00:36:30,146 --> 00:36:31,147
She's on the beach.

298
00:36:32,148 --> 00:36:34,567
She's badly hurt,
but we can still make it.

299
00:36:36,068 --> 00:36:37,320
I should be getting back to her.

300
00:36:37,945 --> 00:36:39,155
You can rest a while.

301
00:36:40,323 --> 00:36:41,949
She'll be safe if she's there.

302
00:36:47,121 --> 00:36:48,581
You and your mother are the same.

303
00:36:52,251 --> 00:36:53,669
Yeah. So I've heard.

304
00:36:53,753 --> 00:36:55,546
You're both close to this island.

305
00:36:57,423 --> 00:36:58,674
Not just close to it

306
00:37:00,760 --> 00:37:01,969
but connected to it.

307
00:37:03,387 --> 00:37:06,474
Tell me, does the island talk to you too?

308
00:37:10,061 --> 00:37:11,812
[sinister music playing]

309
00:37:11,896 --> 00:37:13,814
[man groans]

310
00:37:58,234 --> 00:37:59,151
[man] Diwa.

311
00:38:02,863 --> 00:38:03,781
Diwa.

312
00:38:21,799 --> 00:38:23,801
[water dripping]

313
00:38:28,764 --> 00:38:30,766
[man breathes shakily]

314
00:38:36,105 --> 00:38:37,273
[creature growls]

315
00:38:44,030 --> 00:38:45,239
[whimpers]

316
00:38:54,790 --> 00:38:56,751
- [creature snorts]
- [man breathing shakily]

317
00:39:04,091 --> 00:39:05,718
- [wings flutter]
- [whimpers]

318
00:39:13,184 --> 00:39:14,352
[screeches]

319
00:39:14,435 --> 00:39:16,103
[screams]

320
00:39:17,271 --> 00:39:19,774
[scream echoes]

321
00:39:28,032 --> 00:39:29,867
One must remain.

322
00:39:32,161 --> 00:39:34,246
Another must sacrifice.

323
00:39:36,832 --> 00:39:39,335
You still don't seem to understand.

324
00:39:44,173 --> 00:39:46,092
Why do you think

325
00:39:46,175 --> 00:39:50,388
your mother lasted on this island
for so long?

326
00:39:51,138 --> 00:39:52,473
[scoffs] I don't know.

327
00:39:54,266 --> 00:39:55,893
It's the island.

328
00:39:58,771 --> 00:40:02,066
The island itself
is protecting your mother.

329
00:40:02,149 --> 00:40:05,361
She has a connection to this place
that none of us have,

330
00:40:05,444 --> 00:40:07,154
stronger even than mine.

331
00:40:07,863 --> 00:40:08,864
A connection?

332
00:40:11,742 --> 00:40:13,411
My grandmother told me

333
00:40:15,329 --> 00:40:19,166
that the first person who set foot here
was a woman.

334
00:40:21,210 --> 00:40:22,962
[ominous music playing]

335
00:40:23,045 --> 00:40:26,257
She was shipwrecked too,
like you and your mother.

336
00:40:33,431 --> 00:40:38,644
The first people she gave birth to
became the first people of the island.

337
00:40:39,770 --> 00:40:41,981
They were our ancestors.

338
00:40:49,905 --> 00:40:51,115
You already know

339
00:40:51,198 --> 00:40:54,952
there is something different about us,
the people of this island.

340
00:41:00,708 --> 00:41:03,043
Different. Not wrong.

341
00:41:07,840 --> 00:41:11,051
But to outsiders like the Cardomas,

342
00:41:12,052 --> 00:41:16,891
they may see our differences
as dangerous or unnatural.

343
00:41:18,476 --> 00:41:21,770
But whose job is it to decide who's wrong?

344
00:41:21,854 --> 00:41:24,273
And who can decide who is right?

345
00:41:26,442 --> 00:41:27,693
You tell me who.

346
00:41:37,786 --> 00:41:39,538
Transformations have been rare

347
00:41:39,622 --> 00:41:42,958
ever since Don Ramon and his brothers
have arrived.

348
00:41:44,251 --> 00:41:47,213
They seek to cleanse
our contaminated blood.

349
00:41:51,217 --> 00:41:52,968
<i>Using the holy meat.</i>

350
00:41:53,636 --> 00:41:58,390
All of those who end up here,
all those who die or are dying,

351
00:41:59,141 --> 00:42:00,935
we eat them instead.

352
00:42:03,646 --> 00:42:06,857
It's the only way
to stop us from transforming…

353
00:42:06,941 --> 00:42:08,901
What does all this
have to do with me and my mother?

354
00:42:09,944 --> 00:42:11,028
Sabina.

355
00:42:12,947 --> 00:42:14,698
Have you been listening, child?

356
00:42:17,368 --> 00:42:22,164
Your mother is only the second woman
to come to this island.

357
00:42:25,042 --> 00:42:28,420
- She became one with the--
- I think I've heard enough. I'm…

358
00:42:28,504 --> 00:42:30,839
Did your mother ever tell you
who your father was?

359
00:42:31,966 --> 00:42:35,594
Didn't you feel it in your blood
when you first met Ramon?

360
00:42:35,678 --> 00:42:39,181
- Or when you first landed on this island?
- No, no.

361
00:42:40,683 --> 00:42:44,186
The island, it called to your mother.

362
00:42:44,270 --> 00:42:47,273
The island has brought you to this world.

363
00:42:47,356 --> 00:42:50,442
And now the daughter has returned.
Don't you see?

364
00:42:51,277 --> 00:42:53,112
Don't you understand now?

365
00:42:58,742 --> 00:43:00,744
[Rebecca breathing heavily]

366
00:43:14,300 --> 00:43:15,467
[winces]

367
00:43:26,895 --> 00:43:27,813
Ma.

368
00:43:32,067 --> 00:43:34,403
Wait a second. Let's treat this first.

369
00:43:42,453 --> 00:43:44,872
- Tela gave this to you, didn't she?
- Yeah.

370
00:43:54,673 --> 00:43:57,509
[groans]

371
00:44:03,557 --> 00:44:04,767
[Arturo] That looks like my knife.

372
00:44:05,434 --> 00:44:06,894
Yeah, it is.

373
00:44:06,977 --> 00:44:09,313
You didn't tell me you had a knife.

374
00:44:09,396 --> 00:44:12,483
If I hadn't seen it fall out of your shoe,
I never would have known.

375
00:44:14,276 --> 00:44:16,862
I can't stand not doing anything
to get us out of here.

376
00:44:18,405 --> 00:44:19,740
Help me out here.

377
00:44:19,823 --> 00:44:21,241
Can you see any guards?

378
00:44:22,242 --> 00:44:23,827
No, it's clear. Let's go.

379
00:44:25,871 --> 00:44:27,790
- Try kicking it. Come on.
- Okay.

380
00:44:28,499 --> 00:44:30,000
[grunts]

381
00:44:30,084 --> 00:44:31,710
It's working. Come on, help me.

382
00:44:32,294 --> 00:44:34,213
- [grunts]
- [Arturo] No, wait. Let's do it together.

383
00:44:34,296 --> 00:44:35,756
- One, two, three.
- Two, three.

384
00:44:35,839 --> 00:44:37,341
- [Arturo grunts]
- [Bulak gasps]

385
00:44:38,133 --> 00:44:41,345
Okay, now I'm promoting you to captain.
Good job, Cap.

386
00:44:45,432 --> 00:44:47,434
- [Arturo] Come on. Come on, let's go.
- [Bulak] Okay.

387
00:44:48,519 --> 00:44:50,270
Let's go, Cap. Come on, hurry.

388
00:44:52,022 --> 00:44:54,358
- Hey, come on.
- No, Cap, don't worry about him.

389
00:44:56,110 --> 00:44:56,944
[guard 1] Hey!

390
00:44:59,029 --> 00:45:00,280
What are you doing?

391
00:45:01,657 --> 00:45:04,243
- [Arturo] Just wait.
- Get back in there!

392
00:45:04,326 --> 00:45:05,536
Wait a second, son.

393
00:45:05,619 --> 00:45:07,830
- Get back in there now!
- Just wait.

394
00:45:07,913 --> 00:45:08,997
Right away!

395
00:45:09,081 --> 00:45:10,165
Kid, calm down.

396
00:45:10,749 --> 00:45:12,960
We're not here to hurt you, okay?

397
00:45:13,544 --> 00:45:15,629
Don't come any closer, okay?

398
00:45:18,799 --> 00:45:21,135
- I told you to get back! [yelps]
- Stop!

399
00:45:21,218 --> 00:45:22,761
- [Arturo grunts]
- [guard 1 yelps]

400
00:45:23,429 --> 00:45:25,514
Calm down, okay? Yeah.

401
00:45:25,597 --> 00:45:27,015
[suspenseful music playing]

402
00:45:27,099 --> 00:45:29,101
[footsteps approaching]

403
00:45:31,270 --> 00:45:33,981
- [guard 2] No, wait!
- [guard 1 groans]

404
00:45:34,064 --> 00:45:36,275
[Arturo] Back up now, motherfuckers!

405
00:45:36,900 --> 00:45:39,153
[whimpering]

406
00:45:39,236 --> 00:45:40,946
- [splutters] Please help me.
- Back.

407
00:45:41,738 --> 00:45:43,574
[guard 1 groaning]

408
00:45:45,075 --> 00:45:46,368
- [gunshot]
- [guard 1 shrieks]

409
00:45:47,911 --> 00:45:49,329
- [Bulak] Cap?
- [weapon clatters]

410
00:45:50,164 --> 00:45:50,998
[shrieks]

411
00:45:51,081 --> 00:45:51,957
Cap?

412
00:45:52,040 --> 00:45:54,042
[melancholy music playing]

413
00:45:58,255 --> 00:45:59,089
Cap!

414
00:46:09,600 --> 00:46:10,434
Cap, no.

415
00:46:13,979 --> 00:46:16,398
Cap! Cap! Cap! Cap!

416
00:46:16,482 --> 00:46:18,775
Cap, don't close your eyes.
Don't close them.

417
00:46:18,859 --> 00:46:20,861
[Bulak crying]

418
00:46:21,445 --> 00:46:23,530
[whimpers] Come on. [cries]

419
00:46:24,072 --> 00:46:24,907
Cap.

420
00:46:24,990 --> 00:46:26,742
[crying loudly]

421
00:46:26,825 --> 00:46:27,659
Cap!

422
00:46:27,743 --> 00:46:28,660
[music builds]

423
00:46:28,744 --> 00:46:30,996
Come on. Cap! Cap!

424
00:46:31,079 --> 00:46:31,997
[music fades]

425
00:46:32,080 --> 00:46:34,082
[theme music playing]
